{"id":"b03","n":3,"title_ko":"FAKE LOVE","title_en":"FAKE LOVE","album":"Love Yourself 轉 Tear","year":2018,"yt":"7C2z4GqqS5E","hook":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"notes":{"s":"The love was real to him, and keeping it meant deleting himself.","t":"Lead single of Love Yourself 轉 Tear, May 2018, the album that gave BTS their first number one on the Billboard 200. 轉 is the turn in a four-part Korean narrative structure, and this is where the certainty of DNA breaks: the narrator worked out who the other person wanted and became that, and now there is nobody left behind the performance. The emo-trap production and the collapsing set in the video were a deliberate break from the brightness of the previous era. It was the first BTS single where the hit chorus is an admission of failure, and ARMY reads it as a song about any relationship that runs on performance, including the one with an audience.","k":[["기쁜 척, 강한 척","-(으)ㄴ/는 척하다 is to put on an act of being something. Attach it to an adjective stem for a false front: 모르는 척 pretending not to know, 괜찮은 척 pretending to be fine. The song's whole first verse is built on it, which is why the chorus can call the love fake without ever calling the feeling fake."],["완벽하길, 숨겨지길","-길 is the contraction of -기를, a verb turned into a noun plus the object marker, with the wishing verb 바라다 deleted off the end. What is left is a wish with no one to wish it to, which reads like prayer. Full form 완벽하기를 바라다, I hope it is perfect."],["피울 수 없는 꽃을 키웠어","꽃을 피우다 is the set idiom for bringing something to bloom or making an effort pay off, and 키우다 is to raise or grow. The line pairs them against each other: he kept tending the one thing that by definition was never going to open. Not a translation problem, a contradiction built on purpose."],["아니긴 뭐가 아냐","A slangy self-cancelling frame, X-긴 뭐가 X, roughly what do you mean it isn't, of course it is. The next line runs the same shape on love itself, 사랑은 뭐가 사랑. Worth knowing because the words look like a plain question and the meaning is sarcastic rejection."]]},"vocab":[{"w":"척하다","en":"to pretend, to act as if","i":1},{"w":"슬프다","en":"to be sad","i":1},{"w":"약점","en":"weakness, weak point","note":"약 weak plus 점 point. The opposite, a strong point, is 장점","i":5},{"w":"숨기다","en":"to hide something","note":"숨다 is to hide yourself, 숨기다 is to hide a thing. The -기- in the middle is the causative","i":5},{"w":"이뤄지다","en":"to come true, to be realized","note":"Passive of 이루다, to achieve. Used of dreams and wishes","i":6},{"w":"키우다","en":"to raise, to grow","note":"Covers children, pets, plants and abilities with no change of word","i":7},{"w":"꿈","en":"dream","note":"Both the one you have asleep and the one you chase, as in English","i":6},{"w":"숲","en":"forest, woods","i":16},{"w":"잊어버리다","en":"to forget completely","note":"-어버리다 adds the sense that it is gone for good, often with regret or relief","i":17},{"w":"거울","en":"mirror","i":19},{"w":"지껄이다","en":"to blab, to run one's mouth","note":"Openly rude. Never use it about an elder's speech","i":19},{"w":"대체","en":"on earth, exactly","note":"Drops into a question to add exasperation. A separate noun 대체 means substitute","i":19},{"w":"거짓","en":"lie, falsehood","note":"The literary short form. Spoken Korean says 거짓말","i":29},{"w":"빚어내다","en":"to mold, to craft","note":"빚다 is for shaping clay or kneading rice cake dough. Applying it to lies is the striking part of the line","i":29},{"w":"인형","en":"doll","i":31},{"w":"버리다","en":"to throw away, to abandon","note":"As an ending on another verb it means to do something off completely, as in 잊어버리다","i":42},{"w":"낯설다","en":"to feel unfamiliar, strange","note":"낯 is the face. The opposite is 낯익다, to look familiar","i":44},{"w":"예전","en":"the past, back then","i":45},{"w":"눈멀다","en":"to go blind","note":"In lyrics almost always figurative, blinded by love or greed","i":46},{"w":"모르다","en":"to not know","note":"Irregular, 몰라 and 몰랐어. It is its own verb, not a negated 알다","i":49}],"items":[{"i":0,"ko":"널 위해서라면 난","r":"neol wihaeseoramyeon nan","tk":[{"s":"널","r":"neol","m":[{"t":"널","p":"NP+JKO","pl":"pronoun"}]},{"s":"위해서라면","r":"wihaeseoramyeon","m":[{"t":"위해서","p":"VV+EC+VCP","pl":"verb"},{"t":"라면","p":"EC","pl":"connective ending"}]},{"s":"난","r":"nan","m":[{"t":"난","p":"NP+JX","pl":"pronoun"}]}],"en":"For you, I could"},{"i":1,"ko":"슬퍼도 기쁜 척 할 수가 있었어","r":"seulpeodo gippeun cheok hal suga isseosseo","tk":[{"s":"슬퍼도","r":"seulpeodo","m":[{"t":"슬퍼도","p":"VA+EC","pl":"adjective"}]},{"s":"기쁜","r":"gippeun","m":[{"t":"기쁜","p":"VA+ETM","pl":"adjective"}]},{"s":"척","r":"cheok","m":[{"t":"척","p":"NNG","pl":"noun","en":["pretense, acting like"]}]},{"s":"할","r":"hal","m":[{"t":"할","p":"VV+ETM","pl":"verb"}]},{"s":"수가","r":"suga","m":[{"t":"수가","p":"NNG","pl":"noun","en":["way, chance"]}]},{"s":"있었어","r":"isseosseo","m":[{"t":"있","p":"VA","l":"있다","pl":"adjective","en":["to be","keep"]},{"t":"었","p":"EP","pl":"tense / honorific","g":"past tense"},{"t":"어","p":"EC","pl":"connective ending","g":"casual ending (to a close friend)"}]}],"en":"Pretend to be happy even when I was sad"},{"i":2,"ko":"널 위해서라면 난","r":"neol wihaeseoramyeon nan","tk":[{"s":"널","r":"neol","m":[{"t":"널","p":"NP+JKO","pl":"pronoun"}]},{"s":"위해서라면","r":"wihaeseoramyeon","m":[{"t":"위해서","p":"VV+EC+VCP","pl":"verb"},{"t":"라면","p":"EC","pl":"connective ending"}]},{"s":"난","r":"nan","m":[{"t":"난","p":"NP+JX","pl":"pronoun"}]}],"en":"For you, I could"},{"i":3,"ko":"아파도 강한 척 할 수가 있었어","r":"apado ganghan cheok hal suga isseosseo","tk":[{"s":"아파도","r":"apado","m":[{"t":"아파도","p":"VA+EC","pl":"adjective"}]},{"s":"강한","r":"ganghan","m":[{"t":"강한","p":"VA+ETM","pl":"adjective"}]},{"s":"척","r":"cheok","m":[{"t":"척","p":"NNG","pl":"noun","en":["pretense, acting like"]}]},{"s":"할","r":"hal","m":[{"t":"할","p":"VV+ETM","pl":"verb"}]},{"s":"수가","r":"suga","m":[{"t":"수가","p":"NNG","pl":"noun","en":["way, chance"]}]},{"s":"있었어","r":"isseosseo","m":[{"t":"있","p":"VA","l":"있다","pl":"adjective","en":["to be","ke